model {
  extend basalt.build {
    metadata {
      constraint "A Worker's bundle is the same bytes wherever the checkout and the dependency store sit. Its source map keeps each source's path from the map's own folder, as the bundler writes it, with the two parts that depend on the machine replaced: a dependency in the store is named as if the store sat in the Worker's own package directory, and a module that is not a file keeps its own name instead of a path from the directory the process was started in. A file of the checkout keeps its path, so whatever reads a map from the map's folder still finds it. The bundle's hash covers the map, and an install puts dependencies into a store directory of its own, so without this a plan made in another job saw every Worker as changed although its code was identical. The output folder sits under the directory a build is started in, so two builds agree when they start from the same place in the checkout. A changed source still changes the map and the hash, also when the code built from it stays the same. The change rides in the pinned Alchemy release's dependency patch, so an Alchemy upgrade carries it forward or retires it explicitly."
    }
  }
}
